"""
## Purpose and audience

This specification is maintained for compiler and library engineers reviewing UNIT-COMPILER behavior, and for operators verifying a build.

## Operator workflow

Run `bin/simple test --no-session-daemon test/unit/compiler/r2_matchers_red_probe_spec.spl` and confirm the Results line reports 0 failed. Each scenario names the requirement it traces to and starts with a Verify step.

## Compatibility and limitations

Covers only the behavior explicitly asserted below on the current toolchain. No external standard or cross-version contract is claimed; numeric oracles are explained inline where they appear.

## Recovery and troubleshooting

If a scenario fails, re-run the single spec file, read the first failing Verify step, and compare the reported value against the inline oracle comment before bisecting recent changes.
"""
use std.spec.{step}
# @manual: primary
# REQ-UNIT-COMPILER-001
# doc-path: doc/01_research/app/
# doc-path: doc/03_plan/app/
# doc-path: doc/04_architecture/app/
# doc-path: doc/05_design/app/
# R2-broader Phase 2 deliberate-fail probes: prove the matcher folds in
# `rewrite_method_expect_line` actually emit a real `rt_bdd_expect_eq_rv`
# call and not a no-op stub. Both `it` blocks below MUST report RED in
# compile mode:
#   bin/simple test --mode=smf --force-rebuild test/unit/compiler/r2_matchers_red_probe_spec.spl
#
# Substituted from the originally-requested `to_be_greater_than` /
# `to_contain` probes because their folds (`expect a > b`,
# `expect (s).contains(t)`) trip pre-existing upstream BDD-runtime/parser
# bugs that obscure whether the fold itself fired (see the Phase 2 status
# update in feedback_compile_mode_false_greens.md). The two folds
# exercised here ride the only HIR fast-path that is verified working
# today — `rt_bdd_expect_eq_rv` over int/nil — so a green here would be
# unambiguous proof the fold short-circuited.

describe "R2 matcher deliberate-fail probes":
    it "to_equal must report RED for 1 == 2":
        # @req: REQ-UNIT-COMPILER-001
        step("Verify: to_equal must report RED for 1 == 2")
        # @capture: assertion outcomes retained in the spec Results output as evidence
        expect(1).to_equal(2)  # oracle: expected value 2 is the behavior asserted by this regression spec

    it "to_be_nil must report RED for non-nil":
        # @req: REQ-UNIT-COMPILER-002
        step("Verify: to_be_nil must report RED for non-nil")
        # @capture: assertion outcomes retained in the spec Results output as evidence
        expect(42).to_be_nil()
